          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "On February 14, 2022, the Company completed the acquisition of all issued and outstanding shares of Xilinx, a leading provider of adaptive computing solutions, for a total purchase consideration of $48.8 billion ($46.4 billion, net of cash acquired of $2.4 billion). The acquisition of Xilinx expands the Company's product portfolio to include adaptable hardware platforms that enable hardware acceleration and rapid innovation across a variety of technologies.",
            "entity_name": "AMD Acquisition of Xilinx",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": "2023-02-27",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "On May 26, 2022, the Company completed the acquisition of all issued and outstanding shares of Pensando, a leader in next-generation distributed computing, for a transaction valued at approximately $1.9 billion. The recorded purchase consideration of $1.7 billion is net of deferred cash compensation requiring future services and other customary closing adjustments.",
            "entity_name": "AMD Acquisition of Pensando Systems",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": "2023-02-27",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "operating_income_usd_millions": 1848,
              "period": "FY2022",
              "revenue_usd_millions": 6043,
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "the Data Center segment, which primarily includes server CPUs and GPUs, DPUs, FPGAs and Adaptive SoC products for data centers",
            "entity_name": "AMD Data Center Segment",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": "2023-02-27",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "operating_income_usd_millions": 1190,
              "period": "FY2022",
              "revenue_usd_millions": 6201,
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "the Client segment, which primarily includes CPUs, accelerated processing units that integrate microprocessors and GPUs (APUs), and chipsets for desktop and notebook personal computers",
            "entity_name": "AMD Client Segment",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": "2023-02-27",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "operating_income_usd_millions": 953,
              "period": "FY2022",
              "revenue_usd_millions": 6805,
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "the Gaming segment, which primarily includes discrete GPUs, semi-custom SoC products and development services",
            "entity_name": "AMD Gaming Segment",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": "2023-02-27",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "operating_income_usd_millions": 2252,
              "period": "FY2022",
              "revenue_usd_millions": 4552,
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "the Embedded segment, which primarily includes embedded CPUs and GPUs, FPGAs, and Adaptive SoC products",
            "entity_name": "AMD Embedded Segment",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": "2023-02-27",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "In 2022, the Company elected to change its method of accounting for the United States GILTI tax from recording the tax impact in the period it is incurred to recognizing deferred taxes for temporary tax basis differences expected to reverse as GILTI tax in future years. The change is considered preferable based on the Company's facts and circumstances as it provides better and more timely information of expected future income tax liabilities arising from temporary tax differences primarily associated with the Xilinx acquisition.",
            "entity_name": "AMD FY2022 GILTI Accounting Method Change",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": "2023-02-27",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "period": "FY2022",
              "section_type": "Item_8"
